 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079580 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079580 #edb/ref 1061 701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079580 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fa5bcebe-0da6-5538-9ccd-5d348315d13a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079580 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079581 #edb/ref 1061 703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079581 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a5d43107-12f5-564b-8b7e-258d9b82d9da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079581 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079668 #edb/ref 1064 "We've learned two methods for approximating the value of the derivative at a point by computing the rate of change between two points a distance of $h$ apart, where $h$ is small.\n\n- The forward difference approximation computes the rate of change between the point $x$ and the point $x+h,$ which is a step of $h$ units forward.\n\n$$\nf'(x)  \\approx \\dfrac{f(x+h)- f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n- The backward difference approximation computes the rate of change between the point $x$ and the point $x-h,$ which is a step of $h$ units backward.\n\n$$\nf'(x)  \\approx \\dfrac{f(x)- f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\nNow, we will introduce the **central difference approximation**, also known as the **symmetric difference approximation**. In this approximation, we compute the rate of change between the points $x-h$ and $x+h,$ a distance of $2h$ apart.\n\n$$\nf'(x)  \\approx \\dfrac{f(x+h)- f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n![](images/48/48414a74d6f06fdec0f9b07c2a14f42c3a528b578b3a5f7a61cb4eff93016ac2.png)\n\nUsually, the central difference approximation is a better approximation for $f '(x)$ than the forward difference approximation and the backward difference approximation. This is because for the central difference approximation, $x$ is the midpoint between the two points $x-h$ and $x+h$ that are used in the approximation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079668 #edb/ref 1065 372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079668 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6ac17418-b32e-5d12-97ef-d94adc56f308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079668 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429550 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429550 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 640->993. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429550 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186049236 #edb/ref 17592186045436]}
